        "speaker":  "Louie",
        "time":  "47:29",
        "html":  "The benefits could be company, true company standards. For example, maybe they have a certain work ethic there, and so not only can you bring that standard back. Okay, so you go there, you can work from there, right? Please, could I go? If there\u0027s any room in the budget, let me see the points first. Not only could you copy what\u0027s going on there and bring it back, but you will have... We are starting to build good relationships from the employees from your office to headquarters. It\u0027s like a touch point. People will take notice, and they\u0027ll go, \"What\u0027s going on in that branch?\" The employees are very interested. They want to come here and see what\u0027s going on. It looks like they have progression and promotion in mind. We should keep an eye on that office. They are... Looks like they\u0027re \u003cspan class=\"vocab-mark\" data-vkey=\"initiative\" onclick=\"inspectVocab(\u0027initiative\u0027)\"\u003eseizing the initiative\u003c/span\u003e. Especially if your boss is proposing it as well. For example, if I was in a... For example, I used to do consultations for big companies, right? Big companies in England. I would work with all their sites. They might have eighty sites, and I would know all of them. They would, to try and... With favor with me, they would... They want to come to the site that I\u0027m working on. How can I say? I would have sites, and in these sites, I would train the company\u0027s trainers, right? So then the company\u0027s trainers will train everyone else at the company, and people from smaller sites will want to come and be there, be on that site, try and get in that team. It shows, obviously, for their progression as well, because I do a lot of restructuring for companies because they\u0027re crazy, like in England. We\u0027re so much politics at work, unbelievable. I have no politics. I\u0027m the complete opposite. So they bring me in to do that. Okay, and so what would you say then? Progression, good look on the manager, good relationships and work standards. What would you... Do you have an office admin?"
